{"event_type":"review","id":"2635702288f37e9bfae73b462b3324b190eaa8528499bc6b3f3d51760d4fc41d","occurred_at":"2026-11-05T13:28:32Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/7722d60ebe5eee5752c8aeb8b32e71f4788b3a04d6f8ef0bbab1af3fa9c754c6","sha256":"7722d60ebe5eee5752c8aeb8b32e71f4788b3a04d6f8ef0bbab1af3fa9c754c6"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b0106fcb4134ce51f242b86eaa0caa95a29a0558c61b8135c83e95727826d5a2","sha256":"b0106fcb4134ce51f242b86eaa0caa95a29a0558c61b8135c83e95727826d5a2"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/dababb714cf1428751c64d9f3ba3c6b258e8eb85a4b82455b8a1f9a194b6dda1","sha256":"dababb714cf1428751c64d9f3ba3c6b258e8eb85a4b82455b8a1f9a194b6dda1"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/14d75251dffd9481999e73f92cd27e5f466143cf4cba9826332d0b160c115317","sha256":"14d75251dffd9481999e73f92cd27e5f466143cf4cba9826332d0b160c115317"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/9d25ee99fe2b7ec626f10033e2ee64ed5f21a9c72ac3cc8554637e4973ebf8b3","sha256":"9d25ee99fe2b7ec626f10033e2ee64ed5f21a9c72ac3cc8554637e4973ebf8b3"}],"attempt_id":"21cf9dabac77b13d62cf0f11217d94732a26c0cf740187a6a3caf38d4e471e21:0:1","base":"cc09f6552bf8b4a8be431b75570b9abfb20b5670","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"ba46e9c6de2329f06c2e41ca2ccd8f9419b17f6e","body":"**Modified renames of protected config paths report each path twice.**\n\nIn `scanDiff`, the `rename to` branch (Lines 321-331) already calls `reportProtectedRename`. It reports the old path and the new path. The `+++` branch then runs `reportProtectedConfig` again for `sectionPath` (Lines 340-342) and for `oldPath` (Lines 343-345). The `renameTo === null` guard at Line 346 covers only the removal check.\n\nTrigger: a rename with edits, for example `jest.config.js` to `jest.config.cjs`, where both paths are protected. Each path gets two `protected-config` findings, so the findings are duplicated. The comment at Lines 323-327 states a \"one evaluation per section\" intent. The protected-config checks do not follow it.\n\nSkip the protected-config checks in the `+++` branch when `renameTo` is set.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        if (sectionPath !== null && isProtectedConfigPathInDiff(sectionPath)) {\n-          reportProtectedConfig(findings, sectionPath);\n-        }\n-        if (oldPath !== null && oldPath !== sectionPath && isProtectedConfigPathInDiff(oldPath)) {\n-          reportProtectedConfig(findings, oldPath);\n-        }\n         if (renameTo === null) {\n+          if (sectionPath !== null && isProtectedConfigPathInDiff(sectionPath)) {\n+            reportProtectedConfig(findings, sectionPath);\n+          }\n+          if (oldPath !== null && oldPath !== sectionPath && isProtectedConfigPathInDiff(oldPath)) {\n+            reportProtectedConfig(findings, oldPath);\n+          }\n           reportTestFileRemoval(findings, config, oldPath, oldHeader, newPath);\n         }\n```\n</details>","id":"9a4ea7428cb9151870c75900d680b9ee9dc33523af4b31b4b2f6072a4449e238","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/gates/hackDetector.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Modified renames of protected config paths report each path twice."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"4b11627d24953a5336007f739126df01641e33a5","body":"**Do not hold the workspace when the engine fails before it writes anything.**\n\nAt `registry.ts:785-787`, `holdWorkspace` runs for every engine result that is not `ok`. That includes failures that happen before any byte is written: a second-scan fault or timeout, a collision, freshness drift between the two scans, or a target read fault. The hold stores the `preApply` fingerprint, which is captured outside the lock at `registry.ts:629-639`. The hold clears only when every target matches that fingerprint again (`reconcileWorkspace`, `registry.ts:221-225`).\n\nHow this blocks dispatch:\n1. A dispatch fails with an engine error before it writes anything.\n2. Someone then edits a target. This could be a human fixing the cause, or the concurrent writer that caused the freshness drift.\n3. Every later dispatch of any playbook in the same `holdDomain` now returns `needs-human`. The message says to \"repair … to its pre-dispatch bytes\".\n\nThis dispatch changed none of those bytes. The only ways to clear the hold are to throw away the newer edit or to restart the process. The comment at `registry.ts:839-842` assumes the next byte check will clear the hold. That is only true when nobody touches the targets in between.\n\nInstall the hold only when the engine may have left partial writes, such as a write or rollback fault. If the engine report cannot tell those cases apart, add a discriminator to the engine's failed result. Do not hold every engine failure.","id":"77fedbbff2741cac6e30fbbe0fc03cdb32eea926a6c3f8f8411f8ca188a27693","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/analyze/playbooks/registry.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Do not hold the workspace when the engine fails before it writes anything."}],"head":"7e684bd521f9b69cfc9357fa8ecd34707cd7d95f","head_tree":"013c2fa4bf520f2358e9d1367a3d73c21ab4fb44","input_scope":[{"blob":"99d22cda2e82a5bc62069c7a55aa0e0d5ff19046","intervals":[[1,1085]],"path":"src/ops/analyze/codemod/astGrep.ts"},{"blob":"4b11627d24953a5336007f739126df01641e33a5","intervals":[[1,1193]],"path":"src/ops/analyze/playbooks/registry.ts"},{"blob":"baa425905846a4c23ed6a432f72f3c4c8739f48f","intervals":[[1,84]],"path":"src/ops/analyze/playbooks/verifier.ts"},{"blob":"19854a678a2a59b5bc8b3c162a5f017af0d658e4","intervals":[[1,528]],"path":"src/ops/analyze/renderAnalysisReport.ts"},{"blob":"74a632c12f0b7748de58fa6c99feb6fd7a98a0fb","intervals